LocalAI request-scoped JSON schema forwarding.

Authored against prepared llama.cpp6b4dc2116a92c5c8f2782bfe51fabe5ee66fb5ef.
Both Predict and PredictStream forward Metadata json_schema into the existing
OAI chat-template schema path. Thinking stays enabled; native generated grammar
frames private reasoning and constrains final content, while its PEG parser
returns only final content. No sampler/protobuf changes or output caps.

An explicitly present value must decode to a nonempty object. Malformed,
empty and nonobject schemas fail without echoing raw schema/parser excerpts.
Absent schema leaves existing behavior unchanged. Media uses the same path.
The generic Go boundary also rejects raw grammar plus json_schema. Health advertises
x-you-json-schema=1 as initial gRPC metadata, letting Models fail before Predict
when an older backend lacks support; the Health message stays OK.

Apply to the actually compiled prepared grpc-server.cpp; fail closed if the
pinned source shape differs. The separate CPU fixture exercises real template,
grammar sampler and PEG parser with vocabulary-only loading and no GPU.
